Exp32 result — Track B previous-day range compression -> next-day range expansion: REJECTED. Historical sample used 348 eligible completed broker-days across 71 ISO weeks, split TRAIN 204 days/42 weeks, VALIDATION 72/14, TEST 72/15. TRAIN constant P(next-day expansion)=0.490196. TRAIN fitted k_compress=-0.270934215, odds multiplier=0.762667: after PrevCompress, TRAIN expansion was 42.31% versus 56.00% after non-compressed days. VALIDATION showed the same direction more strongly (30.00% versus 59.38%), but TEST showed essentially no conditional difference (46.15% versus 45.45%). Primary DAY_WEIGHTED whole-ISO-week bootstrap: VALIDATION Brier gain +0.011681455 CI[-0.001856372,+0.026639707], LogLoss +0.023556941 CI[-0.003673213,+0.054723872]; TEST Brier -0.000356433 CI[-0.009291397,+0.008803976], LogLoss -0.000738727 CI[-0.018898917,+0.018076149]. Strict pass=False. The exact 20-day rolling-median one-day compression indicator is closed; no alternate lookbacks, quantiles, compression streaks, direction conditioning, ATR/body/wick/volume substitutions, or interaction rescue. Runtime promotion NONE. Exp27 untouched.

Exp33 frozen — Track B previous-day directional efficiency -> next-day directional continuation. Use completed M5 broker-days strictly before 2026-08-13 00:00 BRT and drop first/last file-edge broker-days. Define day_sign_d=sign(Close_d-Open_d). Define DayEfficiency_d=abs(Close_d-Open_d)/(High_d-Low_d), bounded [0,1] for valid completed days. For target day d, y_continue_d=1 iff day_sign_d==day_sign_{d-1}; feature PrevEfficiency_d=DayEfficiency_{d-1}. Eligible target days require current and prior day_sign non-zero and valid prior efficiency. PrevEfficiencyCentered = PrevEfficiency - TRAIN mean, frozen before OOS. Split whole eligible ISO weeks chronologically 60/20/20; no week may straddle splits. BASE is TRAIN constant P(y_continue=1). EXTENDED freezes BASE and fits exactly one TRAIN coefficient k_efficiency on PrevEfficiencyCentered. Primary unit=completed broker-day; primary estimand=DAY_WEIGHTED; uncertainty=resample whole ISO broker-weeks preserving day weights. Survival requires Brier and LogLoss gain CI95>0 in BOTH Validation and TEST.

Exp33 anti-rescue contract: PrevEfficiency is continuous; no efficiency threshold, quantile, bin, spline, polynomial, body/range variant, wick asymmetry, UP/DOWN coefficient split, streak interaction, range-compression combination, weekday/D1/Clock/Z/Fib/Track-D interaction, or alternate target after result. UP/DOWN prior-day direction may be reported only as descriptive diagnostics and cannot rescue primary failure. If Exp33 fails, close single-day directional-efficiency -> next-day continuation and move to a different predeclared Track-B family. Historical OOS remains exploratory. Exp27 untouched. Runtime promotion NONE.